@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# gpuix-core (local, unpublished)
+
+The complete retained GPUIX renderer without N-API or a Node runtime. This is a
+normal Rust source crate, not a copied renderer snapshot: `src/lib.rs` includes
+shared modules from `packages/native/src`, and both hosts include the same
+`renderer/view.rs`, `renderer/options.rs` and `renderer/retained_tests.rs`.
+
+The existing `gpuix-native` addon keeps its original JS API and default Node
+features. This crate instead uses the GPUI `gpui-pre = 0.3.6` identity used by the
+mobile platform layer. Consumers must source-override that identity at their
+Cargo root to GPUIX's prepared source. Run `node scripts/prepare-gpui.mjs` in
+the GPUIX checkout before invoking Cargo; the mobile CLI does this automatically:
+
+```toml
+[dependencies]
+gpuix-core = { path = "../gpuix/packages/core" }
+
+[patch.crates-io]
+gpui-pre = { path = "../gpuix/.generated/gpui-pre" }
+```
+
+`init(cx)` registers GPUIX input actions/key bindings. `install_host(AsyncApp)`
+installs the foreground application context. `EmbeddedRenderer` supplies the
+existing renderer operations using owned `AsyncApp`/window handles, including
+retained mutation batches and actual native focus, geometry, scroll, text,
+selection, image/font, overlay and automation operations. A native root owns
+`GpuixView`; safe-area/IME effective insets pad the surface in logical pixels.
+The JS engine itself does not belong to a GPUI entity.
+
+**The caller must run its JS engine outside every App/entity update borrow.**
+Native calls enter/leave GPUI synchronously and flush notifications. Root entities
+are not held borrowed across rendering/input operations. Callbacks must enqueue
+JS events, never evaluate JS during paint or native input dispatch. The reusable
+An embedded host implements this ownership/scheduling contract.
+
+The retained view, mutation protocol, styling, text input, markdown/code,
+virtual lists, search/highlights, images/fonts and motion are shared with the
+Node host. Unsupported platform operations return errors (mobile pickers and
+desktop-only window operations); APIs do not fabricate delayed native getters.
+`test-support` enables GPU readback on platforms implementing it. A requested
+capture draws the current scene even if the native frame source is paused for
+an occluded window. It does not simulate OS visibility or OS input.
+
+```sh
+node ../../scripts/cargo-gpui.mjs +stable test --lib --all-features
+```
+
+The shared renderer's 245 library tests passed locally, including retained
+mutation, styling, search/highlight and syntax regressions. This does not by
+itself establish Node backend, desktop OS, or mobile device parity. See the
+frontend mobile tooling for integration validation.
